<title>USA: GM to idle all its Lordstown, Ohio workers.</title>
<headline>GM to idle all its Lordstown, Ohio workers.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp, still feeling the effects of a 20-day Canadian autoworker strike, told all of the approximately 6,000 workers at its Lordstown, Ohio, assembly plant they will be idled until November 10, a spokeswoman for the United Auto Workers union said Thursday.</p>
<p>The plant, which makes the Chevrolet Cavalier and Pontiac Sunfire small cars, has run out of transmissions supplied by a GM parts plant in Windsor, Ontario.</p>
<p>Earlier Thursday, GM said the number of U.S. and Mexican workers sent home because of the strike is 18,801, but that will rise with the Lordstown action.</p>
</text>
